body:
Fixes #3948

## Problem

The composer takes two measurements, and both were keyed only on the draft:

```tsx
// grow the textarea with its content
useLayoutEffect(() => {
  textarea.style.height = 'auto';
  textarea.style.height = `${textarea.scrollHeight}px`;
}, [value, isStacked]);

// decide whether the buttons drop to their own row
useLayoutEffect(() => {
  setIsStacked(ghost.scrollHeight > LINE_HEIGHT_PX);
}, [value]);
```

Neither re-runs when the composer gets wider or narrower without the draft changing. So a draft that fits on one line in a wide window, then wraps after the window is narrowed, keeps the taller stacked layout and textarea height after the window is widened again — until the draft is edited.

## Fix

Observe the column the measuring span lives in and feed its width into both dependency lists:

```tsx
const [composerWidth, setComposerWidth] = useState(0);

useLayoutEffect(() => {
  const column = ghostColumnRef.current;
  if (!column) return;
  const observer = new ResizeObserver((entries) => {
    const entry = entries[0];
    if (entry) setComposerWidth(entry.contentRect.width);
  });
  observer.observe(column);
  return () => observer.disconnect();
}, []);
```

The observed element is the ghost row's inner column (`min-w-0 flex-1`), deliberately **not** the textarea: the textarea's width depends on `isStacked` (it goes `basis-full` when stacked), so observing it would oscillate — the same flip-flop the ghost exists to avoid. The ghost row is laid out side-by-side with fixed `size-9` button stand-ins in both layouts, so its column width depends only on the container. Re-measuring therefore cannot change the observed width and settle into a different value.

`composerWidth` is included in the first effect's deps as well as the second: the height has to be recomputed whenever the line count can change.

## Test

- `pnpm build` (runs `tsc -b` then vite build) — passes.
- `npx eslint src/components/chat/TextInput.tsx` — passes.
- Not verified in a browser: starting the dev server needs approval I don't have in this session, so the resize behaviour was confirmed by reading the dependency graph, not by reproducing in a running app. A reviewer with the UI up can check the issue's repro steps directly.

No frontend test suite exists in `examples/web_ui/frontend`, so no unit test was added.

Fixes #3400

`WordParser` keeps blank paragraphs whose `<w:p>` has no runs, but skipped the ones that still have a run: a paragraph with a single space, or with a run holding just `<w:br/>` from Shift+Enter on an empty line. `_extract_text_from_paragraph()` strips to `""`, so those paragraphs already reach the blank-line branch at `src/agentscope/rag/_parser/_word.py:422`; the run check was what dropped them.

`_is_blank_paragraph()` now decides what Word renders as a blank line. It rejects paragraphs with a `w:drawing`, `w:pict`, `w:object` or OMML math, and any run holding something other than formatting, `<w:br/>`, `<w:cr/>`, tabs or whitespace-only `<w:t>`. Field instructions, symbols and equations therefore still add no line, even though the extractor returns no text for them.

```python
def _is_blank_paragraph(para: DocxParagraph) -> bool:
    root = para._element
    for tag in ("w:drawing", "w:pict", "w:object"):
        if root.findall(".//" + qn(tag)):
            return False
    if root.findall(".//" + _MATH_NS + "oMath"):
        return False

    blank_run_tags = {
        qn(tag)
        for tag in (
            "w:rPr",
            "w:br",
            "w:cr",
            "w:tab",
            "w:lastRenderedPageBreak",
            "w:softHyphen",
        )
    }
    text_tag = qn("w:t")
    for run in root.findall(".//" + qn("w:r")):
        for child in run:
            if child.tag == text_tag:
                if (child.text or "").strip():
                    return False
            elif child.tag not in blank_run_tags:
                return False
    return True
```

The regression tests in `tests/rag_parser_test.py` cover both sides. `test_blank_paragraph_with_a_run_is_preserved` builds `"Paragraph one."`, a space-only paragraph, a break-only paragraph and `"Paragraph two."`; before the change the text section is `'Paragraph one.\nParagraph two.'`, after it is `'Paragraph one.\n\n\nParagraph two.'`. `test_paragraph_with_a_field_code_is_not_a_blank_line` puts a `w:instrText` run between two paragraphs and still expects `'Paragraph one.\nParagraph two.'`.

Verification:

```
$ python -m pytest tests/rag_parser_test.py -q
83 passed, 27 subtests passed

$ uvx black==23.3.0 --line-length=79 --check src/agentscope/rag/_parser/_word.py tests/rag_parser_test.py
2 files would be left unchanged

$ uvx flake8==6.1.0 --extend-ignore=E203 src/agentscope/rag/_parser/_word.py tests/rag_parser_test.py
```

No public API change. Documents containing these paragraphs keep a blank line instead of losing it.
